{"name":"Embroidery","hex":"#d4bebf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"embroidery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The art of decorating fabric or other materials using a needle to stitch thread or yarn.","The ornamentation of fabric using needlework."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embroidery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Embroidery","blocks":[{"text":"Embroidery is the art of decorating fabric or other materials using a needle to stitch thread or yarn. It is one of the oldest forms of needlework, a type of textile art, with origins dating back thousands of years across various cultures. Common stitches found in early embroidery include the chain stitch, buttonhole or blanket stitch, running stitch, satin stitch, and cross stitch. Modern embroidery continues to utilize traditional techniques, though many contemporary stitches are exclusive to machine embroidery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Kantha_%28Quilt%29_LACMA_AC1994.131.1.jpg/330px-Kantha_%28Quilt%29_LACMA_AC1994.131.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embroidery"},{"title":"Embroidery (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Embroidery  is an active Japanese Thoroughbred racehorse best known for winning the 2025 Oka Sho, 2025 Shūka Sho, and 2026 Victoria Mile. At the end of her 2025 season, she was awarded the JRA Award for Best Three-Year-Old Filly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Embroidery-2025-10-19b.jpg/330px-Embroidery-2025-10-19b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embroidery_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Alice_Maywood_sampler_-_DPLA_-_0e5b4f600d63fe8366c20c2ce5a90ec4_%28page_1%29.jpg/500px-Alice_Maywood_sampler_-_DPLA_-_0e5b4f600d63fe8366c20c2ce5a90ec4_%28page_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.w